        {
            "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
            "body": "Just add a bit more context to the OP. Even in 0.12 release, using `shellslash` can trigger the same issue. The root cause is that a C program's [`argv[0]`](https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/cpp/c-language/parsing-c-command-line-arguments) typically represents the program path or name (e.g. `C:/windows/system32/cmd.exe`). `cmd.exe` is a bit unusual in that it parses `argv[0]` and treats `/c` as a switch, which causes the launch to [fail](https://github.com/neovim/neovim/pull/37729#discussion_r3145397976).\r\n\r\n",
